# Static chat UI

Single HTML file, no CSS/JS framework. Header / scrollable chat / footer. No CDN scripts.

## Viewport shell

The document MUST NOT scroll. Use `html, body { height: 100%; height: 100dvh; overflow: hidden }`. Header and footer `flex-shrink: 0`. Chat (`#chat`) is the only vertical scroller: `flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto`.

`min-height: 100dvh` on `body` lets the page grow and the browser pan the whole document when the on-screen keyboard opens (header and last bubble disappear). Prefer a fixed viewport height plus `visualViewport` to match the visible area.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — document can grow; keyboard pans the page */
body { min-height: 100dvh; }
#chat { flex: 1; overflow-y: auto; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
html, body { height: 100%; height: 100dvh; overflow: hidden; }
header, footer { flex-shrink: 0; }
#chat { flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; }
```

## Bot replies

Render a Markdown subset with `createElement` / `textContent`. MUST NOT assign the model reply to `innerHTML` or `insertAdjacentHTML`. User and system bubbles stay plain text.

## Mobile chrome

On viewports ~360–480px the composer MUST stay compact. Do not leave a large empty gap between the farewell hint and the input.

`flex-basis` follows the flex direction. A value meant as **width** in a row (`flex: 1 1 12rem`) becomes **height** if the same rule sits on a column. Override it in the column media query (`flex: 0 0 auto` or drop the basis).

```css
/* ❌ BAD — 12rem is height once the toolbar is a column */
.toolbar span { flex: 1 1 12rem; }
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .toolbar { flex-direction: column; }
}

/* ✅ GOOD */
.toolbar span { flex: 1 1 12rem; min-width: 0; }
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .toolbar { flex-direction: column; }
  .toolbar span { flex: 0 0 auto; }
}
```

Keep footer padding and toolbar gaps tight on small screens. Prefer wrapping or stacking controls over hiding the farewell hint or “Nueva consulta”.
